Subject: The animation timer stays off while the display link draws every refresh

While an animation runs (a region scroll, a custom shader's loop), the display link draws at
every refresh, and the renderer thread also armed its animation timer every 8 ms
(`draw_interval_ms`). Under vsync the timer's draw does nothing (`Thread.drawFrame` leaves
drawing to the display link then), so each tick only woke the thread to arm the next one.

A draw wake is no longer armed while the display link runs. Once a draw stops the link (no
animation needs every refresh any more; with 0016, a region scroll slowing to rest),
`drawNowCallback` arms the timer again, so the frames still due come from it. Update wakes
(Kitty animations, which need the frame data rebuilt) are armed as before.

Measured in Calm (headless Debug app, M5 Pro, 2026-10-06, with and without this patch, one round
each): region scrolls streaming a step every 0.1 s, 996 interrupt wakeups a second before and
204 after, 195 and 187 million instructions; scrolls coming to rest, 378 and 123 wakeups, 148
and 144 million; a pane redrawing every refresh (a cursor shader's loop), 775 and 204 wakeups,
118 and 116 million. Frames presented stay the same (303 and 305 over eight scrolls to rest,
each still moving its whole 102 px; 420 and 416 streaming; 480 and 479 in four seconds of the
loop).

Calm's own patch (not from thdxg/ghostty); applies on top of 0005–0016. No Zig test: the
decision is in the renderer thread's event loop, which needs a surface; the frame check is a
self-test (DESIGNS.md → Motion in the terminal).

diff --git a/src/renderer/Thread.zig b/src/renderer/Thread.zig
--- a/src/renderer/Thread.zig
+++ b/src/renderer/Thread.zig
@@ -530,6 +530,11 @@
     // Draw immediately
     const t = self_.?;
     t.drawFrame(true);
+
+    // The draw stops the display link once no animation needs every
+    // refresh; one still under way (a region scroll slowing to rest)
+    // goes on with the timer.
+    if (!t.renderer.hasVsync()) t.armAnimationTimer();
 
     return .rearm;
 }
@@ -595,6 +600,11 @@
 /// actual next wake.
 fn armAnimationTimer(self: *Thread) void {
     const wake = self.renderer.animationWake() orelse return;
+    // While the display link runs it draws at every refresh, and a draw
+    // wake would find nothing to do (drawFrame leaves drawing to vsync
+    // then): it only woke the thread every 8 ms. drawNowCallback arms
+    // the timer again once the link stops.
+    if (wake.kind == .draw and self.renderer.hasVsync()) return;
     self.animation_wake = wake.kind;
     self.render_h.reset(
         &self.loop,
